{"name":"Holiday Velvet","hex":"#206174","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"holiday","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A day on which a religious event or secular celebration is traditionally observed.","A day declared free from work by the state or government."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take a period of time away from work or study.","To spend a period of time in recreational travel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holiday"},{"term":"velvet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A closely woven fabric (originally of silk, now also of cotton or man-made fibres) with a thick short pile on one side.","Very fine fur, including the skin and fur on a deer's antlers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with velvet or with a covering of a similar texture.","To coat raw meat in starch, then in oil, preparatory to frying."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/velvet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Holiday","blocks":[{"text":"A holiday is a day or other period of time set aside for festivals or recreation. Public holidays are set by public authorities and vary by state or region. Religious holidays are set by religious organizations for their members and are often also observed as public holidays in religious majority countries. Some religious holidays, such as Christmas, have become secularised by part or all of those who observe them. In addition to secularisation, many holidays have become commercialised due to the growth of industry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Lathmar_Holi_2022_in_Nandgaon%2C_Uttar_Pradesh_%28edited%29.jpg/330px-Lathmar_Holi_2022_in_Nandgaon%2C_Uttar_Pradesh_%28edited%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holiday","wikidata":"Q1445650"},{"title":"Velvet","blocks":[{"text":"Velvet is a type of woven fabric with a dense, even pile that gives it a distinctive soft feel. Historically, velvet was typically made from silk. Modern velvet can be made from silk, linen, cotton, wool, synthetic fibers, silk-cotton blends, or synthetic-natural fiber blends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velvet","wikidata":"Q243519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg/500px-Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg/1280px-Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg/500px-Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChamps-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg/500px-School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg/1280px-School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg/500px-School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASchool_C